IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulations 13 and 14, both "for the purposes of section 14
-- of the Act" (income estimated for a year in which the income of the applicant or the applicant's spouse or common-law partner
-- falls): the month in which a loss of income occurs (13) and what counts as pension income (14).
--
-- "The month" is answered as the first day of that month, a DATE, because the Regulations name a month, not a day, and the
-- keel's month helpers work on dates.

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Month in which Loss of Income Occurs`

-- 13(a)(i): the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment is the month in which the last day in respect of
-- which he receives income from it falls. The day is the last day for which income is received, which is not always the day
-- the work stopped.
-- src:106 | 13 For the purposes of section 14 of the Act,
-- src:107 | (a) the month in which an applicant or an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner
-- src:108 | (i) ceases to hold an office or employment shall be the month in which the last day in respect of which he receives income from that office or employment falls, or
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 13(a)(i) (src:106-108)
GIVEN `the last day in respect of which the person receives income from the office or employment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 13(a)(i): the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment` `the last day in respect of which the person receives income from the office or employment` MEANS
    `the first day of the month containing` `the last day in respect of which the person receives income from the office or employment`

-- 13(a)(ii): the month in which the person ceases to carry on a business is the month of the last day on which he actively
-- carries it on.
-- src:109 | (ii) ceases to carry on a business shall be the month in which the last day on which he actively carries on that business falls; and
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 13(a)(ii) (src:109)
GIVEN `the last day on which the person actively carries on the business` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 13(a)(ii): the month in which the person ceases to carry on a business` `the last day on which the person actively carries on the business` MEANS
    `the first day of the month containing` `the last day on which the person actively carries on the business`

-- 13(b): the month of a loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income is the month in which the termination or
-- reduction actually occurs.
-- src:110 | (b) the month in which an applicant or an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner suffers a loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income shall be the month in which that termination or reduction actually occurs.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 13(b) (src:110)
GIVEN `the day on which the termination or reduction of pension income actually occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 13(b): the month in which the person suffers a loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income` `the day on which the termination or reduction of pension income actually occurs` MEANS
    `the first day of the month containing` `the day on which the termination or reduction of pension income actually occurs`

§§ `Definition of Pension Income`

-- 14: "pension income" is the aggregate of the amounts received as (a) to (i). Two limbs carve something out of their own item: (e)
-- "other than a death benefit" and (f) "other than a benefit received pursuant to the Act or any similar payment received pursuant to
-- a law of a provincial legislature". The record keeps the gross amount of those two items and the amount carved out of it, so that
-- the carve-out is done by the rule. Every amount is a non-negative number of dollars.
-- src:113 | 14 For the purposes of section 14 of the Act, pension income means the aggregate of amounts received as
-- src:114 | (a) annuity payments;
-- src:115 | (b) alimony and maintenance payments;
-- src:116 | (c) employment insurance benefits;
-- src:117 | (d) disability benefits deriving from a private insurance plan;
-- src:118 | (e) any benefit, other than a death benefit, under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan as defined in the Canada Pension Plan;
-- src:119 | (f) superannuation or pension payments, other than a benefit received pursuant to the Act or any similar payment received pursuant to a law of a provincial legislature;
-- src:120 | (g) compensation under a federal or provincial employee’s or worker’s compensation law in respect of an injury, disability or death;
-- src:121 | (h) income assistance benefits under an agreement referred to in subsection 33(1) of the Department of Human Resources Development Act by reason of a permanent reduction in the work force as described in that subsection; and
-- src:122 | (i) income assistance benefits under the Plant Workers’ Adjustment Program, the Fisheries Early Retirement Program or the Northern Cod Adjustment and Recovery Program by reason of a permanent reduction in the work force.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 14 (src:113-122)
DECLARE `reg 14: Amounts received` HAS
    `reg 14(a): annuity payments`                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(b): alimony and maintenance payments`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(c): employment insurance benefits`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(d): disability benefits deriving from a private insurance plan`                          IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(e): benefits under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan as defined in the Canada Pension Plan` IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(e): of which a death benefit`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(f): superannuation or pension payments`                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(f): of which a benefit received pursuant to the Act or any similar payment received pursuant to a law of a provincial legislature` IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(g): compensation under a federal or provincial employee's or worker's compensation law in respect of an injury, disability or death` IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(h): income assistance benefits under an agreement referred to in subsection 33(1) of the Department of Human Resources Development Act by reason of a permanent reduction in the work force as described in that subsection` IS A NUMBER
    `reg 14(i): income assistance benefits under the Plant Workers' Adjustment Program, the Fisheries Early Retirement Program or the Northern Cod Adjustment and Recovery Program by reason of a permanent reduction in the work force` IS A NUMBER

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 14 (src:113-122)
GIVEN amounts IS A `reg 14: Amounts received`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 14: pension income` amounts MEANS
        amounts's `reg 14(a): annuity payments`
    PLUS amounts's `reg 14(b): alimony and maintenance payments`
    PLUS amounts's `reg 14(c): employment insurance benefits`
    PLUS amounts's `reg 14(d): disability benefits deriving from a private insurance plan`
    PLUS (amounts's `reg 14(e): benefits under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan as defined in the Canada Pension Plan` MINUS amounts's `reg 14(e): of which a death benefit`)
    PLUS (amounts's `reg 14(f): superannuation or pension payments` MINUS amounts's `reg 14(f): of which a benefit received pursuant to the Act or any similar payment received pursuant to a law of a provincial legislature`)
    PLUS amounts's `reg 14(g): compensation under a federal or provincial employee's or worker's compensation law in respect of an injury, disability or death`
    PLUS amounts's `reg 14(h): income assistance benefits under an agreement referred to in subsection 33(1) of the Department of Human Resources Development Act by reason of a permanent reduction in the work force as described in that subsection`
    PLUS amounts's `reg 14(i): income assistance benefits under the Plant Workers' Adjustment Program, the Fisheries Early Retirement Program or the Northern Cod Adjustment and Recovery Program by reason of a permanent reduction in the work force`
